{"at":"2026-11-26 18:57","message":"SUPABASE_DB_URL in .env is now well-formed but still uses the direct host (db.<ref>.supabase.co), which does not resolve on this IPv4-only network (ENOTFOUND). Do this: 1) Supabase dashboard > your project > Connect > choose 'Session pooler' (not 'Direct connection') and copy the URI, which looks like postgresql://postgres.<ref>:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres (the user part is postgres.<ref>, not plain postgres). 2) Put your database password in place of [YOUR-PASSWORD], URL-encoding special characters (+ is %2B, $ is %24, @ is %40). 3) Replace the SUPABASE_DB_URL line in .env with that whole string, no spaces or trailing comment. 4) Check with: node tools/smoke-realtime.mjs (expect 4 passed), then re-run: node run_phases.mjs. Everything else in 01-setup is done and passing (repo pushed, app scaffolded, realtime OK, 20/20 iTunes previews)."}